    "create_time": 1786599026.563,
    "update_time": 1786599032.279176,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "> **Limitations.** Our data come from a single course at one institution. To probe generalization, we applied the classifier without retraining to a second offering of the course with different TAs and assignments. Macro-F1 fell from 0.72 to 0.66, and F1 for *stalled-after-error* from 0.68 to 0.61, suggesting that some features (e.g., assignment-specific error types) do not transfer. We did not evaluate other courses, languages, or institutions, and expect larger drops where error vocabularies differ. Labels were produced by three authors familiar with the course. Although agreement was substantial (Light's κ = 0.71), the labels encode our reading of student behavior rather than students' own accounts of being stuck. Finally, the TA study (n = 6) measured perceived prioritization and time-to-visit within lab sessions, not learning outcomes.\n\n148 words. The last sentence pre-empts the \"does this help students learn?\" question that will come up at the talk."
     ]
    },
